class:: PinkTrombone
summary:: Full Pink Trombone articulatory voice model with separate audio outputs
categories:: UGens>Generators>PhysicalModels
related:: Classes/Formant, Classes/Klank

description::
A native port of Neil Thapen's Pink Trombone, modularized by Christian d'Heureuse.
Implements the LF glottis, aspiration and simplex modulation, 44-cell mouth,
28-cell nose, tongue shaping, multiple constrictions, frication, and plosive
transients. The tract runs twice per output sample. Returns four audio signals:
code::[mixed voice, mouth, nose, glottis]::. Select element 0 for normal listening.

The default 512-sample internal model cadence matches the upstream browser.
It does not depend on the server block size. All ordinary controls accept numbers,
control-rate UGens, or audio-rate UGens. LF coefficients update on waveform cycles;
shape and pitch targets update at model boundaries. Use code::modelBlockSize: 1::
for per-sample target updates. This requires more CPU and changes the original
block-dependent smoothing behavior.

The supplied macOS binaries support Apple Silicon and Intel, scsynth and supernova.
They are ad-hoc signed, not Developer ID signed or Apple notarized.

classmethods::
method:: ar
argument:: freq
Target fundamental in Hz, default 140. Clipped to 10 through 0.2 times sample rate.
argument:: tenseness
Target glottal tenseness, 0 to 1, default 0.6.
argument:: tongueIndex
Tongue position in oral cell coordinates, 0 to 43, default 12.9. Typical range 12 to 29.
argument:: tongueDiameter
Tongue shape diameter, 2.05 to 3.5, default 2.43.
argument:: velum
Nasal opening diameter, default 0.01. The original open value is 0.4.
argument:: gate
Positive means the glottis is touched. Default 0. Set alwaysVoice to 0 to use gate
for note release. Releasing does not free the Synth.
argument:: alwaysVoice
Default 1, keeps the source sounding without a touch.
argument:: autoWobble
Default 1, enables the two large simplex pitch variations. Small pitch and tenseness
noise remain when this is 0.
argument:: vibratoAmount
Sinusoidal fractional pitch depth, 0 to 1, default 0.005.
argument:: vibratoFrequency
Sinusoidal vibrato rate in Hz, 0 to 100, default 6.
argument:: aspiration
Aspiration noise multiplier, 0 to 10, default 1.
argument:: frication
Turbulence noise multiplier, 0 to 10, default 1.
argument:: excitation
External audio added to the glottal input of the tract, default 0.
argument:: glottisGain
Internal glottis gain entering the tract, 0 to 10, default 1. Set 0 to use only external
excitation. The separate glottis output is unaffected by this gain.
argument:: glottalReflection
Glottal boundary reflection, default 0.75, clipped to -0.999 through 0.999.
argument:: lipReflection
Lip and nostril termination reflection, default -0.85, clipped to -0.999 through 0.999.
argument:: movementSpeed
Wall movement speed, default 15, range 0 to 1000. Zero freezes the current shape.
argument:: transientTrig
Positive-going trigger starts an additional transient. Automatic closure-release
transients remain active independently.
argument:: transientPosition
Oral cell 0 to 43 for manual transient, default 30.
argument:: transientStrength
Manual transient initial strength, default 0.3, range 0 to 10.
argument:: transientLife
Manual transient lifetime in seconds, default 0.2, range 0 to 10.
argument:: transientExponent
Manual transient decay exponent, default 200. Amplitude is strength times
code::2.pow(exponent.neg * age)::.
argument:: reset
Positive-going trigger clears acoustic and filter state and rewinds the seeded noise.
argument:: seed
Initial numeric constant, integer 0 to 16777215, default 1. Use separate seeds for independent voices.
argument:: modelBlockSize
Initial numeric constant, integer 1 to 512, default 512. Independent of server block size.
argument:: diagnostics
Initial numeric constant, 0 or 1. Default 0 returns four channels. 1 returns 148 channels.
argument:: aspirationNoise
External signal feeding the original 500 Hz aspiration bandpass, when enabled by externalNoise.
argument:: fricationNoise
External signal feeding the original 1000 Hz frication bandpass, when enabled by externalNoise.
Held across both tract substeps and each point's noise consumption.
argument:: externalNoise
Bitmask: 0 uses both internal noise sources, 1 external aspiration, 2 external frication, 3 both external.
argument:: noiseModulator
Negative (default -1) uses glottal turbulence modulation. 0 to 1 overrides it.
Aspiration retains its own original modulation.
argument:: diameters
Array of exactly 44 oral target diameters, numbers or signals. Default all -1.
Nonnegative values override individual targets (0 to 10); negatives use the tongue shape.
Constrictions are applied after these overrides. Use NamedControl.kr for setn access.
argument:: noseDiameters
Array of exactly 28 nasal diameter overrides. Default all -1. Element 0 overrides
the velum target; other cells change at model boundaries. Custom nasal profiles
recalculate nasal reflections. With no overrides, upstream's fixed nasal reflections are retained.
argument:: constrictions
Array of up to 64 code::[index, diameter, gate]:: triples. Default empty. Changes shape
and injects turbulence. Diameter is the original touch diameter; the constricted target
subtracts 0.3. A diameter near 0.5 produces frication, and 0.3 or less can close the tract.
A negative diameter below -0.8 beyond cell 17 opens the velum, as in the browser.
argument:: turbulencePoints
Array of up to 64 additional code::[index, diameter, gate]:: triples, with noise injection
only. Default empty. Gates have the source's 100 ms noise attack/release. Released points
retain their last coordinates during the tail. Reusing a slot restarts its touch.

returns::
Four OutputProxy objects, or 148 with diagnostics enabled. Ordinary scalar control
arrays expand into multiple voices. Diameter arrays and point triples describe cells
and points of one voice and do not expand into separate voices.

discussion::
Output map (zero based):
table::
## 0 || Mixed voice, original 0.125 two-substep summation gain.
## 1 || Mouth only, at the same gain as its contribution to output 0.
## 2 || Nose only, at the same gain as its contribution to output 0.
## 3 || Raw glottal source with aspiration, before glottisGain and external excitation.
## 4-47 || Oral cell amplitude envelopes, when diagnostics are enabled.
## 48-75 || Nasal cell amplitude envelopes.
## 76-119 || Current oral cell diameters.
## 120-147 || Current nasal cell diameters.
::

Output 0 equals output 1 plus output 2 to rounding precision. Diagnostics contain
envelopes and geometry; they are not speaker feeds. No limiter or DC blocker is
inserted. Use an appropriate output gain, especially with raw glottis or transients.

The original 44/28-cell lengths remain unchanged at different sample rates, so
formants vary with sample rate as in the original. Each instance uses about 0.55 MiB
of server real-time memory, mostly for its two repeating noise buffers. Increase
code::s.options.memSize:: before booting for many voices. Up to 256 simultaneous
transients are retained; excess events retire the oldest. Nonfinite inputs use defaults.

See the package's docs/PARAMETERS.md and docs/SOURCE_ANALYSIS.md for input bounds,
timing details, source mapping, and real-time adaptations.

examples::
code::
s.boot;
x = { PinkTrombone.ar(autoWobble: 0)[0].dup * 0.4 }.play;
x.free;

// Move the tongue and open the nose.
x = {
    var voice = PinkTrombone.ar(
        tongueIndex: SinOsc.kr(0.2).range(12, 29),
        tongueDiameter: SinOsc.kr(0.13).range(2.1, 3.3),
        velum: LFPulse.kr(0.5).range(0.01, 0.4), autoWobble: 0
    );
    (voice[0] * 0.3).dup
}.play;
x.free;

// A repeating fricative touch, with its 100 ms attack and release.
x = {
    PinkTrombone.ar(constrictions: [[30, 0.5, LFPulse.kr(2)]])[0].dup * 0.3
}.play;
x.free;

// Process another audio source through the tract.
x = {
    PinkTrombone.ar(
        glottisGain: 0, excitation: Saw.ar(100) * 0.1,
        tongueIndex: SinOsc.kr(0.2).range(12, 29),
        tongueDiameter: 2.2, autoWobble: 0
    )[0].dup
}.play;
x.free;
::
